WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning John!

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:04.330
So a little while ago, I went on Google, and
I was going to ask the question, "What is

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.230
the difference between something and something?".

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:09.490
But I didn't get that far because I noticed
how interesting all the questions other people

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:10.490
were asking were.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.610
So having forgotten completely what I was
going to ask Google, instead, today I'm just

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.970
going to answer all of the questions other
people were asking for every letter of the

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:18.970
alphabet.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.970
Starting with: A.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.770
Crows and ravens are two completely different
species.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:24.940
If there's a bunch of them and they're acting
and sounding pretty annoying, those are crows.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.700
If there's one or two of them, and you think,
"Is that a cat, because it's huge," that's

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.700
a raven.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.800
Baking soda is the chemical sodium bicarbonate.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.160
It produces carbon dioxide when mixed with
an acid, and that carbon dioxide fluffs up

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.160
baked goods.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.550
Baking powder is baking soda with the acid
already mixed in, so all you have to do is

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.550
add water.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.440
In the US, a college is a school that teaches
only the years directly after secondary education.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.750
A university has some graduate school components.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.290
To make things extra confusing, both colleges
and universities can contain other colleges.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.110
Dinner vs. supper is a really interesting
linguistic thing that happened.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.720
Apparently, supper means a different thing
to EVERYONE.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.600
English people and things are from England,
which is a country inside the country of the

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.600
United Kingdom.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.360
British people and things technically are
anything from the United Kingdom, so Northern

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.961
Irish people, Welsh people, Scottish people:
all British - though they probably don't want

00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:09.961
to be called that.

00:01:09.961 --> 00:01:11.830
Hair and fur are, scientifically, the exact
same thing.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:15.430
Hulu Plus costs more, and you can watch it
on your TV or your mobile device.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.840
There's also very slightly more content on
Hulu Plus.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.450
The 5C is the, kind of, value edition of the
iPhone.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.820
The camera and the processor and the design
are all a little bit less fancy.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.370
Jelly is jellied juice and jam is jellied
fruit pulp, so jam is a little bit softer.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.210
As with anything in linguistics, this is surprisingly
complicated, but both kun and san are Japanese

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.210
honorific suffixes.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.229
They're added to the end of names to show
respect.

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:40.130
San is used between equals, while kun is used
in reference to someone junior to you, generally

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.159
a male person.

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:45.310
LCD is the kind of display technology, LED
is the kind of back-lighting the TV has.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:49.561
They have nothing to do with each other, and
these days, most TVs are LCD displays back-lit

00:01:49.561 --> 00:01:50.561
by LED.

00:01:50.561 --> 00:01:52.970
I mean, biologically, there's very little
difference between you and me.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.229
Humans are all very, very similar to each
other.

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:57.600
I have no idea what NAS and SAN are.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.020
I looked it up, and it's something to do with
IT infrastructure, and sorry, out of my depth

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.020
there.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.280
Subjective statements are based in opinion;
objective statements are based in fact.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.289
This first one makes no sense, so I'm gonna
skip it.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:12.140
Prisons are where you go when you've been
convicted of a crime and sentenced to serve

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.140
time.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.950
Jails are where you go when you've just been
detained or have been arrested and are awaiting

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:16.950
trial.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.790
You can also end up in a jail if you've been
convicted but your sentence isn't very long.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.510
Both full and quick formats will wipe all
the data off your hard drive, but only the

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.120
full format will rebuild the file structures
that the drive itself uses to store the files

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.850
and scan for bad sectors on the drive.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.510
Both Rangers and Green Berets are special
operations forces in the Army.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.060
Any recruit can apply to be a Ranger, but
only soldiers who have been in the army for

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.010
at least three years can apply to be a Green
Beret.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.190
Green Berets must also speak at least two
languages.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.950
The duties performed by both groups, though,
are similar.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.220
Scotch is a type of whiskey.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.480
It's Scotch, meaning that it's made in Scotland.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.709
"Too" either means "excessively" or "also."

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:47.379
"To" is just for all the other times, unless
you mean "two."

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:50.040
As far as I can tell, Uber and Lyft are pretty
much the same thing.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.879
They're both new-fangled ways to get taxis,
and people seem surprisingly excited about

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:56.209
both considering that taxis will be mostly
driven by robots in ten years.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.959
Green cards give you the right to permanently
live and work in the US, while visas only

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:01.459
temporarily give you that right.

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:04.819
Green and white asparagus are the same plant,
but white asparagus has dirt piled on top

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:06.989
of it while it's growing, so that it's never
exposed to light.

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:10.240
Under all that dirt, it doesn't produce chlorophyll,
and it doesn't need the structures necessary

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:14.910
to stand up on its own, so it's milder in
flavor and softer in texture.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:19.950
x64 is the 64-bit CPU architecture for Windows
7 that works on newer machines, while x86

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.940
is the older 32-bit design.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:24.840
Green and yellow zucchini are different colors.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:25.840
And finally,

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:26.890
A zucchini is a squash!

